Having a personal homepage has always been a desire of mine, yet I’ve never actually had one. As a web developer, I knew exactly what I wanted, but there were always lingering questions that needed answers.

-   Which technologies do you want to use?
-   Why don’t you use the ready-made templates?
-   Are they good enough? Do they fit your needs?
-   Why not use free services?
-   …

The questions and doubts are endless, and they always left me disappointed in the early steps. This time I started by writing down my basic requirements for a simple home page, and finally, it worked for me!

I built this blog from scratch, ~using Remix, React, and MUI~ as the presentation layer, while utilizing the WordPress API via GraphQL. If you’re interested in reviewing the [`source code`](https://github.com/a-ahandani/remixpress) or using it for yourself, feel free to fork it.

~To get a glimpse of how different elements come together, you can check out the demo page.~

If there were any unclear parts, please don’t hesitate to contact me.
